    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: the $4.00 no-show cancellation fee stands, and the driver is paid $3.20 of it as compensation.\n\nArrival. The platform GPS trace places the driver inside the 120 m pickup geofence at the ION Orchard PHV bay with 40 qualifying fixes; the policy requires only three. So the driver had arrived (POL-NS-01(b), POL-NS-02). The rider's point that the 'arrived' tap at 18:44:30 was 15 seconds ahead of the first qualifying in-geofence fix at 18:44:45 does not defeat the charge: a false marker requires the driver to have been either more than 300 m from the pin or travelling at 15 km/h or more at the marker, and neither is shown (POL-NS-05). A slightly early tap is expressly not a technicality that voids an otherwise good fee.\n\nWaiting time. You are right, rider, that the car never stood still for five unbroken minutes — the two spells at the bay were 170 seconds (18:44:45-18:47:35) and 185 seconds (18:49:35-18:52:40). But POL-NS-06(i) expressly allows those separated spells to be added where a lawfully enforced kerb restriction made holding position impossible: the LTA advisory on file is a bus-lane / no-stopping restriction covering Orchard Road and Orchard Turn from 17:00 to 20:00, its geometry covers the pickup point, its window covers the whole wait, and the driver never went further than 179 m from the pin, inside the 300 m leash. Added together his in-geofence time is 355 seconds against the 300-second minimum for a large-venue pickup, so there is no shortfall and the waiting-period rule in POL-NS-06 does not return the fee. The 2-minute loop away from the bay (18:47:35-18:49:35) is not counted as waiting time; the driver's own message at 18:47:50 shows the marshal moved him on, not that he abandoned the pickup. On the accumulated basis the required waiting time was complete at 18:51:45, so the 18:52:45 cancellation came after it (POL-NS-01(d)).\n\nThe rider is not exonerated by POL-NS-04. The driver replied to her message within 90 seconds, inside the 120-second limit, so that clause does not apply regardless of content; and independently her own device sat 690-717 m from the pickup pin, outside the 150 m rider-presence radius, through the whole window.\n\nCompensation and amount. POL-NS-07 gives the driver 80% of the $4.00 fee, i.e. $3.20, with 20% retained as platform fee. The anti-farming guard does not bite: 2 no-show terminations in 30 days is below the threshold of 4, and 2/118 is 0.017, far below 0.08, so both limbs fail and no escalation arises. The $4.00 charged also reconciles with the fee schedule — the greater of the $4.00 large-venue fee and the $4.00 RYDE_X tier fee — so there is no fare defect (POL-NS-08(d)). Profile facts other than the counters the policy names for this category (driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d and completed_trips_30d) were treated as background only and carry no weight.\n\nOutcome: the rider's $4.00 charge is not refunded; the driver is paid $3.20. No referral is made, because no clause produces one on these facts (the arrival was genuine, so POL-NS-05(ii) does not fire).",
    "referrals": []
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 3.20,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 3.20,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Outcome: the $4.00 no-show fee stands as charged, and the driver is paid $3.20 of it under POL-NS-07. Both money fields carry the same figure because that is the amount this ruling moves (POL-GEN-03); it is not a refund to the rider.\n\nTo the rider. Your description of the car moving about is factually correct, and I have not treated it as mistaken: the trace shows the driver holding the ION Orchard bay for 170 seconds (18:44:45-18:47:35), leaving for about two minutes, and holding it again for 185 seconds (18:49:35-18:52:40). He never stayed five unbroken minutes in one place. However, POL-NS-06(i) lets those two spells be added together where the driver left and re-entered the arrival radius without ever travelling more than 300 m from the pin AND a kerb restriction of the listed type was in force on the pickup road. Both conditions hold on the platform's own numbers: his furthest point during the loop was 179.0 m from the pin (inside the 300 m leash), and LTA's traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00214-01 (KERB_RESTRICTION, full-day bus lane on Orchard Road/Orchard Turn 17:00-20:00, geometry covering the pickup road and window covering the whole wait) means holding the kerb was not lawfully possible. That is the very thing the driver told you at 18:47:50 and what the marshal enforced. The effective dwell is therefore 170 + 185 = 355 seconds against the 300-second LARGE_VENUE minimum, a surplus of 55 seconds. On your specific points: (i) your reading that the clock cannot start before the first in-geofence fix at 18:44:45 is accepted - POL-NS-01(c) measures the dwell from the first qualifying fix, not the 18:44:30 tap - but it does not change the result, because 355 seconds still clears 300; (ii) your point that a fresh 300 seconds from 18:49:35 would not have run by the 18:52:45 cancellation is right only if the earlier 170 seconds are discarded, and POL-NS-06(i) says they are summed, so the minimum was reached at about 18:51:45, before the cancellation; (iii) your point that the fee is earned by the waiting period and not by your conduct is correct as a principle, but the waiting period was served, so POL-NS-06's refund route is not engaged. POL-NS-04 does not help you either: the driver answered your 18:46:20 message at 18:47:50, inside the 120-second limit, so the no-reply condition fails, and your own trace places your device 690-717 m from the pin throughout, outside the 150 m large-venue presence radius. POL-NS-06 does not require a refund, and none is due.\n\nTo the driver. The fee is chargeable under POL-NS-01: an 'arrived' event exists (18:44:30); the trace places you inside the 120 m LARGE_VENUE arrival radius with 40 qualifying fixes; the effective dwell measured from the first qualifying fix is 355 seconds against the 300-second minimum; and the trip was terminated by you at 18:52:45 with no boarding event and reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW, at or after the moment the minimum elapsed. No clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it. POL-NS-03 does not apply because you were inside the arrival radius rather than outside it, and in any event registered_pickup_points is 1, so the pin-ambiguity goodwill branch is unavailable. POL-NS-05 is not triggered: nothing places you more than 300 m from the pin or travelling at 15 km/h or above at the arrival timestamp, and the 15-second earliness of the tap is the harmless kind POL-NS-05(iii) describes, the clock simply being recomputed from 18:44:45. POL-NS-06 finds no shortfall. POL-NS-08 shows no impairment of any artifact that carries the decision: no clock skew (the arrival event sits within 5 seconds of a fix), no trace gap (100% coverage, maximum gap 0 seconds, 83 fixes), the chat numbering and count reconcile with trip_record.chat_message_count, and the $4.00 fee reconciles with the greater of the LARGE_VENUE zone fee ($4.00) and the RYDE_X tier fee ($4.00), so POL-NS-08(d) is not engaged. POL-NS-07 therefore pays you 80% of the fee, $3.20, with the residual $0.80 retained as the platform service fee. The anti-farming guard does not bite: no_show_terminations_30d is 2 (below 4) and 2/118 completed trips is 0.017 (below 0.08), so both limbs fail and no escalation arises under POL-NS-09. The profiles were used only as POL-GEN-01 permits - driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d and completed_trips_30d for the POL-NS-07 check - and no finding rests on any context-only field. No clause on this record produces a referral."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 3.20,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 3.20,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "Both parties: the $4.00 no-show charge stands, and the driver is paid 80% of it ($3.20). Here is why, point by point.\n\nRIDER — your main complaint, that the car kept moving and never held the bay for five minutes, is factually borne out by the GPS trace: the driver's two stops inside the 120 m ION Orchard pickup zone lasted 170 s (6.44.45–6.47.35pm) and 185 s (6.49.35–6.52.40pm), and his longest single stop was 185 s, not five minutes. But the policy does not ask for one continuous stop here. POL-NS-06(i) lets the two in-zone stops be added together where the driver never went more than 300 m from the pin and a kerb restriction made it unlawful to hold position. Both conditions are met: the LTA bus-lane advisory (no stopping 5–8pm on Orchard Road / Orchard Turn between Paterson Rd and Bideford Rd) covers the pickup road and the whole wait, and the driver's furthest point on his loop was 179 m from the pin. The effective wait is therefore 170 + 185 = 355 seconds, comfortably over the 300-second (5-minute) minimum for a large-venue pickup, and the derived shortfall is minus 55 seconds. Your argument that the 120 seconds away 'was not waiting' cannot be accepted — that gap is exactly what limb (i) exists to allow when the law forces the driver off the kerb, and the driver said so in the chat at 6.47.50pm. Your second point, that the 6.44.30pm 'arrived' tap came 15 seconds before the first in-zone fix at 6.44.45pm, also does not change the outcome: the marker is not a false arrival under POL-NS-05 (no fix over 300 m and no reading at 15 km/h or more at the marker), and in any event the waiting clock runs from the first qualifying in-zone fix, which still yields 355 seconds. Your third point, that the driver cancelled before the required dwell elapsed, fails once the stops are summed: 300 seconds of in-zone wait was reached at 6.51.45pm and the cancellation was at 6.52.45pm, so limb (d) is met.\n\nRIDER — POL-NS-04 does not exonerate you. The driver answered your 'ok coming down now' message at 6.47.50pm, within 120 seconds, so limb (b) is not met; and your own device sat between 690 m and 717 m from the pickup pin for the entire window, with no qualifying fix inside the 150 m rider-presence radius, so limb (c) fails affirmatively. POL-NS-03 does not apply either: the pickup has a single registered point (so pin ambiguity is unavailable) and the driver's holds were inside the arrival zone, not at a wrong face of the building.\n\nDRIVER — your account matches the record: you were at the bay, the advisory explains why you had to leave the kerb, and you were back within about 120 seconds. POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it, so POL-NS-07 pays you 80% of the $4.00 fee, i.e. $3.20, the remaining $0.80 being retained as the platform service fee. On a DRIVER_COMPENSATION ruling the amount field carries that same $3.20; it is not a refund to the rider, whose $4.00 charge stands. The anti-farming guard does not bite: 2 no-show terminations in 30 days (threshold 4) and a rate of 2/118 = 1.7% (threshold 8%).\n\nNo artifact is impaired: the trace has 100% coverage with no gap in the waiting window, the chat is complete and matches the trip record's message count, the fare reconciles with the fee schedule (greater of the $4.00 zone fee and the $4.00 tier fee), and the driver's track is intact. The case is therefore decided at full weight, confidence is above the 0.70 floor, and no escalation or referral is required."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
